It's not the 'undiggable' flag (which is tested after the subsequently
described tests), rather the test for the stairs is explicitly coded
in the source. There are at least two checks that could be triggered
in the same condition where monster use wands; nr 1 is the already
mentioned "furniture" check, and nr 2 is a test of the monster
coordinates against some stairs coordinates:
   sstairs.sx == mtmp->mx && sstairs.sy == mtmp->my
(though I haven't checked what these 'sstairs' actually are). Both
tests will lead to the result
   pline_The("digging ray is ineffective.");
and the dig command returns unsuccessfully.

I checked it also in wizard mode, and you'll get as expected:
"The gnome zaps a wand of digging!  The digging ray is ineffective."

So I'd hesitate talking about a bug as long as the OP hadn't provided
more information about the circumstances, and first of all, about the
version he played. _If_ he was not mistaken in the first place.

